dwight kurt schrute has shown himself to  be at various points both terribly  misguided and an unexpected voice of  reason on the office more often than you  might expect the eccentric beat farmer  and assistant to the regional manager  played by rayne wilson on the classic  nbc sitcom is actually worth listening  to despite his strangeness dwight often  shows a knack for problem solving and  critical thinking that proves  indispensable in the workplace at one  point he brings a spud gun into work in  a duffel bag just to test the office  park's security who else would take that  initiative plus he's all about loyalty  but if there were somewhere else that  valued that loyalty more highly  i'm going wherever they value loyalty  the most  don't think about that one too hard by  all accounts particularly his own dwight  is a force to be reckoned with and an  asset to be paid attention to but the  people around dwight don't regard him  this way very often or at all really  dwight isn't actually treated fairly in  most instances his boss and idol michael  scott repeatedly spurns him both in  terms of friendship and the promotions  dwight craves consider michael's rolodex  entry on dwight which reads simply quote  tall beats might dwight the resident  weirdo of the office be as  underappreciated hero there are many  signs that point to this being true but  something that happens during the office  season 2 really drives this point home  here's the office conflict that has fans  reevaluating dwight and jim of course  nobody wants to dislike the big hero jim  and it is entertaining to watch dwight  swing wildly between oblivious  incompetence frustration and genuine  dominance where he uses his intelligence  to command the situation and the people  in it over time however it's hard not to  notice how often dwight has met with  dismissiveness and even full-on  antagonism no matter how he behaves  that's not to say he doesn't sometimes  instigate problems himself the incessant  prank war between dwight and jim halpert  the time dwight put the entire office in  real danger to prove a point about being  prepared in the event of a fire the  verbal jabs he throws at his fellow  dunder mifflin employees that's just the  tip of the iceberg but the issue is that  dwight isn't always to blame and when he  feels uncomfortable at work and turns to  his company for help he is at best  laughed at at worst he's ignored one of  the worst examples of the lack of  respect dwight gets comes from human  resources representative toby flenderson  in the season 2 episode conflict  resolution the episode sees dwight  approaching toby with some very  legitimate claims about jim's behavior  it's toby's job to hear dwight out  address his concerns appropriately and  resolve the conflict between dwight and  jim unfortunately toby neglects him  sticking all of dwight's complaints in a  box rather than taking them seriously  the office is a comedy of course but if  we're thinking in terms of real-life  companies toby's actions are almost  certainly a violation of procedure and  outside of a professional context it's  just a jerk move as many fans have  pointed out toby kind of lets everyone  down in the episode as it reveals that  he's kept a massive file of unresolved  complaints from dunder mifflin employees  held back but is particularly hard on  dwight who's clearly complained about  jim for years and been ignored basically  every time sure dwight's a lot to handle  on his own but if an employee is that  concerned about a co-worker ignoring it  probably isn't the best response dwight  is visibly distressed by jim's actions  he doesn't find jim's antics funny and  the show doesn't depict their prank war  as harmless fun between friends jim's  behavior messes with dwight's sense of  his own sanity his emotions and his  ability to do his job at one point jim  even tricks him into going into the  women's restroom this adds up to a  textbook hostile work environment but  toby never lifts a finger to do what he  is literally paid to do fans of the  office are now looking back on the  episode and feeling sympathy for dwight  seeing him as a complicated character  who deserves some kindness here  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite tv shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Applause]  [Music]
 

